# CI-01 — Pipeline de deploy de Lambdas (`apps/rag_lmbd_*`)

## Objetivo

Crear el workflow `.github/workflows/deploy-lambdas.yml` que detecta **qué Lambdas cambiaron**
en un push a `main` / `tenant_boletin` y despliega **sólo las afectadas** haciendo
`aws lambda update-function-code` con un ZIP construido on-the-fly.

No usar Terraform en este pipeline. El módulo `terraform/modules/lambda` ya gestiona
la configuración (VPC, env vars, IAM). Este workflow sólo actualiza el código.

---

## Lambdas en scope

Cada directorio bajo `apps/` con prefijo `rag_lmbd_` es una Lambda independiente.
Lista actual (puede crecer — el pipeline debe ser dinámico, no hardcodeada):

| Directorio (`apps/<dir>`)        | Función Lambda (`<dir>-<env>`)                        |
|----------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|
| `rag_lmbd_alert_creation`        | `rag_lmbd_alert_creation-<env>`                       |
| `rag_lmbd_anmatlinks`            | `rag_lmbd_anmatlinks-<env>`                           |
| `rag_lmbd_anmatlinks_reset`      | `rag_lmbd_anmatlinks_reset-<env>`                     |
| `rag_lmbd_bolinks`               | `rag_lmbd_bolinks-<env>`                              |
| `rag_lmbd_dbwriter`              | `rag_lmbd_dbwriter-<env>`                             |
| `rag_lmbd_embeddings`            | `rag_lmbd_embeddings-async-<env>` *(nombre especial)* |
| `rag_lmbd_embeddings_enqueue`    | `rag_lmbd_embeddings_enqueue-<env>`                   |
| `rag_lmbd_fetcher`               | `rag_lmbd_fetcher-<env>`                              |
| `rag_lmbd_notifier`              | `rag_lmbd_notifier-<env>`                             |
| `rag_lmbd_obtener_alertas`       | `rag_lmbd_obtener_alertas-<env>`                      |
| `rag_lmbd_parser`                | `rag_lmbd_parser-<env>`                               |
| `rag_lmbd_query`                 | `rag_lmbd_query-<env>`                                |
| `rag_lmbd_query_dispatcher`      | `rag_lmbd_query_dispatcher-<env>`                     |
| `rag_lmbd_s3writer`              | `rag_lmbd_s3writer-<env>`                             |
| `rag_lmbd_stepfunction`          | `rag_lmbd_stepfunction-<env>`                         |

> **Convención de nombre:** `<dir>-<env>`, donde `<env>` viene del branch o variable.
> Excepción ya documentada: `rag_lmbd_embeddings` → `rag_lmbd_embeddings-async-<env>`.
> Agregar excepciones similares en un mapa `FUNCTION_NAME_OVERRIDE` dentro del script.

---

## Lógica de detección de cambios

```
on push → git diff HEAD^ HEAD → paths que empiecen con apps/rag_lmbd_*
          → extraer lista de directorios únicos afectados
          → para cada uno: build ZIP + update-function-code
```

Usar `actions/checkout@v4` con `fetch-depth: 2` para tener el commit anterior.

Script bash de detección (paso `detect-changes`):

```bash
CHANGED=$(git diff --name-only HEAD^ HEAD | grep '^apps/rag_lmbd_' | cut -d/ -f1-2 | sort -u)
echo "lambdas=$(echo $CHANGED | tr '\n' ' ' | jq -Rc 'split(" ") | map(select(length > 0))')" >> $GITHUB_OUTPUT
```

Si `lambdas` es un array vacío `[]`, los pasos de deploy hacen early-exit (`if: steps.detect.outputs.lambdas != '[]'`).

Añadir también `workflow_dispatch` con un input `lambda_dir` (string, opcional):
si está presente, forzar deploy de esa Lambda ignorando el diff.

---

## Estructura del workflow

```
jobs:
  detect:       → produce matrix de lambdas afectadas
  deploy:       → matrix job: build ZIP + update-function-code
                   needs: detect
                   strategy.matrix.lambda: ${{ fromJson(needs.detect.outputs.lambdas) }}
```

### Job `detect`

```yaml
detect:
  runs-on: ubuntu-latest
  outputs:
    lambdas: ${{ steps.diff.outputs.lambdas }}
  steps:
    - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      with:
        fetch-depth: 2
    - id: diff
      name: Detect changed lambdas
      run: |
        # Si es workflow_dispatch con lambda_dir override, usarlo directamente
        if [[ -n "${{ inputs.lambda_dir }}" ]]; then
          DIRS='["apps/${{ inputs.lambda_dir }}"]'
        else
          CHANGED=$(git diff --name-only HEAD^ HEAD \
            | grep '^apps/rag_lmbd_' \
            | awk -F/ '{print $1"/"$2}' \
            | sort -u)
          if [[ -z "$CHANGED" ]]; then
            DIRS='[]'
          else
            DIRS=$(echo "$CHANGED" | jq -Rc '[., inputs]' | jq -sc '.')
            # forma segura:
            DIRS=$(echo "$CHANGED" | jq -Rsc 'split("\n") | map(select(length > 0))')
          fi
        fi
        echo "lambdas=$DIRS" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
```

### Job `deploy`

```yaml
deploy:
  needs: detect
  if: needs.detect.outputs.lambdas != '[]'
  runs-on: ubuntu-latest
  strategy:
    fail-fast: false          # una lambda rota no cancela el resto
    matrix:
      lambda_dir: ${{ fromJson(needs.detect.outputs.lambdas) }}
  env:
    AWS_REGION: ${{ vars.AWS_REGION || 'us-east-1' }}
    ENVIRONMENT: ${{ vars.DEPLOY_ENVIRONMENT || 'prod' }}
  steps:
    - uses: actions/checkout@v4

    - name: Configure AWS credentials (OIDC)
      uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@v4
      with:
        role-to-assume: ${{ secrets.AWS_BATCH_ECR_ROLE_ARN }}
        aws-region: ${{ env.AWS_REGION }}

    - name: Set up Python 3.12
      uses: actions/setup-python@v5
      with:
        python-version: "3.12"

    - name: Build ZIP
      id: build
      run: |
        DIR="${{ matrix.lambda_dir }}"
        LAMBDA_BASENAME=$(basename "$DIR")
        DIST="$DIR/dist"
        ZIP_PATH="$DIST/${LAMBDA_BASENAME}.zip"

        rm -rf "$DIST" && mkdir -p "$DIST"

        # Instalar dependencias si existe requirements.txt
        if [[ -f "$DIR/requirements.txt" ]]; then
          pip install --upgrade pip --quiet
          pip install -r "$DIR/requirements.txt" -t "$DIST" --quiet
        fi

        # Copiar fuentes
        cp "$DIR"/*.py "$DIST/" 2>/dev/null || true
        if [[ -d "$DIR/lib" ]]; then
          mkdir -p "$DIST/lib"
          cp "$DIR/lib/"*.py "$DIST/lib/" 2>/dev/null || true
        fi

        cd "$DIST"
        zip -r "${LAMBDA_BASENAME}.zip" . > /dev/null
        cd -

        echo "zip_path=$ZIP_PATH" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
        echo "lambda_basename=$LAMBDA_BASENAME" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"

    - name: Resolve function name
      id: fn
      run: |
        BASENAME="${{ steps.build.outputs.lambda_basename }}"
        ENV="${{ env.ENVIRONMENT }}"

        # Mapa de overrides (formato: "dirname:function_name_sin_env")
        declare -A OVERRIDES=(
          ["rag_lmbd_embeddings"]="rag_lmbd_embeddings-async"
        )

        if [[ -n "${OVERRIDES[$BASENAME]+x}" ]]; then
          FUNCTION_NAME="${OVERRIDES[$BASENAME]}-${ENV}"
        else
          FUNCTION_NAME="${BASENAME}-${ENV}"
        fi

        echo "function_name=$FUNCTION_NAME" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"

    - name: Deploy to Lambda
      run: |
        aws lambda update-function-code \
          --function-name "${{ steps.fn.outputs.function_name }}" \
          --zip-file "fileb://${{ steps.build.outputs.zip_path }}" \
          --region "${{ env.AWS_REGION }}"

    - name: Wait for update to complete
      run: |
        aws lambda wait function-updated \
          --function-name "${{ steps.fn.outputs.function_name }}" \
          --region "${{ env.AWS_REGION }}"

    - name: Summary
      run: |
        echo "✅ Deployed \`${{ steps.fn.outputs.function_name }}\` from \`${{ matrix.lambda_dir }}\`" \
          >> "$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY"
```

